<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimated Wednesday 100,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimated Wednesday 100,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts Wednesday were 100,000 head, compared with 111,000 a week ago and 92,000 a year ago.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were $0.50 per cwt lower than mid-session Tuesday. Trade and demand light to moderate.</p>
<p>Offerings moderate.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    55.00 -56.00	   56.00 -57.00</p>
<p>few			54.50  56.50		    57.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    54.00 -56.00	   54.50 -57.00</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
